// Tests for the 3 remaining uncovered parser functions.
// All 3 are blocked by compiler codegen bugs (verified 2026-03-07):
//
// 1. parse_socket_addr -- SEGFAULT at runtime. The function body contains both
//    SocketAddr::V4(...) and SocketAddr::V6(...) constructors. The V6 path
//    creates a SocketAddrV4 from the V6 port via SocketAddr::V6(), which triggers
//    an access violation during struct conversion codegen.
//    Even importing and calling this function (error path only) crashes.
//
// 2. SocketAddrV6::parse -- "Type mismatch: expected SocketAddrV6, found ()"
//    Static method defined in parser.tml's `impl SocketAddrV6` block.
//    Cross-module static method dispatch resolves return type as () instead of
//    the actual Outcome[SocketAddrV6, AddrParseError].
//
// 3. SocketAddr::parse -- "Unknown method: is_ok" on the return value.
//    Delegates to parse_socket_addr. Cross-module static method dispatch fails
//    to resolve the Outcome return type, so methods like is_ok() are not found.
//
// The underlying free functions (parse_socket_addr_v4, parse_socket_addr_v6)
// are fully covered in parser_ipv4.test.tml, parser_ipv6.test.tml, etc.
use test::{assert}

@test
func test_parser_remaining_blocked() -> I32 {
    assert(true, "parse_socket_addr, SocketAddrV6::parse, SocketAddr::parse blocked by codegen bugs")
    return 0
}
